%% W1D5 — Episodic vs. Semantic Memory — Request Flow
%% Shows the full lifecycle: user turn → memory retrieval → working memory
%% assembly → LLM call → async episodic write → session-close promotion trigger.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant Agent as Agent Runtime
    participant Router as Memory Router
    participant EpiDB as Episodic Store
    participant SemDB as Semantic Store
    participant LLM as LLM GPT-4o-mini
    participant Pipeline as Promotion Pipeline

    User->>Agent: Submit query (session_id, user_id, text)
    Agent->>Router: Route memory retrieval (query, user_id, token_budget=2000)

    Router->>EpiDB: Hybrid search (filter: user_id, top_k=3, score=0.7*sim+0.3*recency)
    EpiDB-->>Router: Top-3 episodic events with scores

    Router->>SemDB: Relevance search (query embedding, top_k=2)
    SemDB-->>Router: Top-2 semantic facts with confidence scores

    Note over Router: Enforce token budget:\nepisodic <= 1200 tokens\nsemantic <= 800 tokens

    Router-->>Agent: Assembled memory context (episodic block + semantic block)

    Agent->>LLM: Prompt = system + memory context + current turn
    Note over LLM: Memory blocks wrapped in\nstructural delimiters\nto prevent prompt injection

    alt Response generated successfully
        LLM-->>Agent: Generated response text + token usage
        Agent-->>User: Return response
        Agent-)EpiDB: Async write: serialise event (user_id, session_id, timestamp, content, embedding)
        Note over Agent,EpiDB: Fire-and-forget — does not\nblock the user response
    else LLM call fails or times out
        LLM-->>Agent: Error or timeout
        Agent-->>User: Fallback response (graceful degradation)
        Agent-)EpiDB: Async write: error event with metadata
    end

    Note over User,Agent: Session continues for N turns\n(steps 1-12 repeat per turn)

    User->>Agent: Session close signal
    Agent-)Pipeline: Trigger promotion job (session_id, resolved=true)
    Note over Pipeline: Runs async — does not\nblock session close response

    Pipeline->>EpiDB: Fetch resolved events (last 24h, unprocessed)
    EpiDB-->>Pipeline: Batch of episodic events

    Pipeline->>Pipeline: Cluster events by semantic pattern

    alt Cluster has >= 3 independent events
        Pipeline->>LLM: Summarise cluster into candidate semantic fact
        LLM-->>Pipeline: Candidate fact text
        Pipeline->>Pipeline: Validate fact (length, non-contradiction, confidence)
        Pipeline->>SemDB: Write validated fact (text, provenance_ids, valid_until TTL)
        Note over SemDB: Fact available for\nnext session retrieval
    else Cluster has < 3 events
        Pipeline->>Pipeline: Skip promotion — insufficient evidence
    end
